    content: "\u003cp\u003eA common query among government job aspirants is whether an \u003cstrong\u003eOnline BBA degree\u003c/strong\u003e satisfies official recruitment qualifications for government examinations. Here is the legal breakdown.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eGovernment Equality Clause\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe University Grants Commission (UGC) mandates that online degrees from recognized Category-I and NAAC-accredited universities are equivalent to regular campus degrees for all public sector hiring and government jobs.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eEligible Recruitment Exams\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUPSC Civil Services Examination (IAS/IPS/IFS)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSSC CGL (Combined Graduate Level)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBanking Recruitment (SBI PO, IBPS Probationary Officer)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eState Public Service Commissions (State PSC)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eMake sure to maintain minimum required graduation percentages as specified in exam notifications.\u003c/p\u003e"
