    excerpt: "Clarifying entrance exam rules: Learn why UGC-DEB approved Online BBA degrees meet 100% eligibility criteria for CAT, XAT, MAT, NMAT, and IIM admissions.",
    content: "\u003cp\u003eA crucial question among management aspirants is whether an \u003cstrong\u003eOnline BBA degree\u003c/strong\u003e qualifies them to sit for the CAT exam and gain admission into top IIMs or foreign B-Schools. Here are the facts.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eOfficial Eligibility Criteria\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eUnder UGC guidelines, any 3-year bachelor\u0027s degree granted by a recognized university (online or regular) with at least 50% marks makes a candidate 100% eligible for competitive post-graduate entrance exams including CAT, XAT, SNAP, and CMAT.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eCareer Path to MBA\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCAT \u0026 IIM Admissions:\u003c/strong\u003e Fully Accepted\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eXLRI, FMS, SPJIMR, MDI:\u003c/strong\u003e Fully Eligible\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eForeign University Masters/MBA:\u003c/strong\u003e Eligible with WES Evaluation\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eAlways verify your university\u0027s UGC-DEB status on the official DEB portal before applying.\u003c/p\u003e"
