    content: "\u003cp\u003eBefore enrolling in any online program, ensuring regulatory compliance is essential. Here is a guide to the \u003cstrong\u003eUGC-DEB 2026 Regulations\u003c/strong\u003e for Online BBA degrees.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003e1. NAAC Score Mandate\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eOnly universities accredited by NAAC with a minimum \u0027A\u0027 grade or recognized Category-I Autonomous status can offer full online degrees.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003e2. Equal Status Notice\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eUnder UGC Section 22(1), online degrees granted in accordance with UGC Regulations are at par with campus degrees for employment and higher education.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003e3. Online Proctored Examinations\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eTerm-end semester exams are conducted securely via AI-proctored online platforms or designated exam centers.\u003c/p\u003e"
